Cell["\<\
-------- Original Message --------
Subject: Re: RegionMeasure[x^2 + y^2 <= a^2]
Date: Thu, 24 Oct 2013 17:10:17 -0500
From: Adam Strzebonski <adams@wolfram.com>
To: Eric Weisstein <eww@wolfram.com>

The definition of RegionCentroid requires that the dimensions
of the measure and of the region agree, so it cannot take
a dimension argument. RegionCentroid will work for regions that
depend on symbolic parameters when we have code for computing
integrals over such regions. Currently RegionMeasure[R, n] defaults
to Integral[Boole[implicit description of R], vars] when n is equal
to the embedding dimension, and fails for other n.

Adam\
\>", "Text"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Closed]],

